cent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.1.stable, 4.5.beta5\n- Not reproducible in: 4.3.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta5 - Fedora Linux 42 (Adams) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (RADV GFX1201) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 60.39 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhenever you pull in changes to your project that includes new resources, from something like Git, while having the editor still open, you will always end up with errors like:\n\n```\nUnrecognized UID: \"uid://d0pi376alu7e6\"\n```\n\nThe UIDs in question always seem to correspond to the new files that were part of the changes pulled in through VCS.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the MRP\n2. Minimize the editor\n3. Run `git checkout 114a38b39` in the MRP directory (which just adds a `main.gd` resource)\n4. Restore the editor\n5. Note errors about \"Unrecognized UID\"\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[unrecognized-uid.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21794225/unrecognized-uid.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api